WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.640
"Stranger Things 4" Vol. 1 ends with&nbsp;
a massive cluster of cliffhangers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:08.800
Vecna's identity is revealed, but he&nbsp;
still hasn't unveiled the extent of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:13.200
his master plan – and he's also far from&nbsp;
the only threat out there. Fortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:18.720
answers are just around the corner in the&nbsp;
super-sized final episodes of "Stranger Things 4."

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.640
"He's not going to stop – not&nbsp;
until he's taken everyone."

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:28.320
After keeping a demogorgon at bay with nothing&nbsp;
but a lit torch and sheer intimidation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:33.360
Jim Hopper has had a weapons upgrade, and&nbsp;
he looks like he's handling it just fine.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:38.080
Cutting through at the 1:30 mark of the trailer,&nbsp;
the heroic Hopper stands tall wielding what looks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:43.200
to be a sword cool enough to make Conan the&nbsp;
Barbarian jealous. His specific location isn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:48.240
that clear, but chances are he's still in Russia&nbsp;
searching for a way home. In the grand scheme of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:52.800
things, it's an interesting weapon of choice for&nbsp;
the former lawman, especially considering the fact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:58.240
that everyone else in the trailer is tooling up&nbsp;
with shotguns and flamethrowers – go nuts, Murray.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:03.200
Hopper himself also wields a gun elsewhere in the&nbsp;
trailer. This suggests to us that Hopper is likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:08.800
facing off against some human opposition in this&nbsp;
shot, rather than the Upside Down's hardier stock.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:12.960
With that said, in a show that's made&nbsp;
Dungeons and Dragons an unofficial guide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:17.360
to battling supernatural forces, it makes&nbsp;
sense that someone is finally going to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:22.080
a sword to do some damage. Who better than&nbsp;
Eleven's fatherly knight in shining armor?

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:26.880
Vol. 2 of "Stranger Things 4" will&nbsp;
undoubtedly lead Eleven to go for a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:32.640
rematch against Henry Creel, aka the horrifying&nbsp;
slasher villain Vecna. The only question is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:37.360
whose turf will it take place on? We can't say&nbsp;
for sure, but the trailer offers tantalizing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:41.840
hints that Eleven will be returning home —&nbsp;
both in the right-side-up and the upside-down.

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:47.040
Judging by the latest teaser, we see Eleven out&nbsp;
in the open air, away from the test facility she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:52.400
was confined to in Vol. 1. We also get a final&nbsp;
glimpse of El returning to where it all began:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:57.840
the Creel home. Has she come to save Max, Lucas,&nbsp;
and Erica, who look to have headed there as well?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:02.480
Or is this the final showdown that will close the&nbsp;
door on Vecna for good? Place your bets, folks.

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:08.080
Just in case Jim Hopper and company aren't having&nbsp;
a miserable enough time with just one demogorgon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:13.040
Vol. 2 of season 4 sets them up against&nbsp;
more than one invader from the Upside Down.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:17.760
Toward the end of the trailer, viewers are&nbsp;
treated to a brief shot of a demodog tearing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:21.600
through the corridors of the Russian&nbsp;
prison, apparently chasing Hopper.&nbsp;

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:26.240
Familiar from the second season of "Stranger&nbsp;
Things," the demodogs are the second-to-last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:30.480
development stage of the demogorgon. While&nbsp;
they're significantly smaller and weaker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:35.120
than the adult creature, they're still highly&nbsp;
dangerous and can do a lot of damage, as poor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:40.080
Bob Newby and a whole bunch of lab workers found&nbsp;
out during the second season of "Stranger Things."

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:43.760
Unless it somehow turns out to be&nbsp;
Dustin's semi-friendly former pet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:48.640
Dart, the presence of a demodog in the&nbsp;
prison is highly concerning. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:53.520
it means that the adult demogorgon isn't the&nbsp;
only one in the complex. Will this be the sole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:58.240
demodog in there, or will Hopper, Joyce, and&nbsp;
the others have to deal with an entire pack?

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:03.760
The back half of the trailer really ramps up&nbsp;
the action, and includes a surprising moment in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:09.920
which Lucas throws a solid punch at his teammate&nbsp;
Jason in an attic drenched in blue light. It's not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:14.000
surprising that these two have finally come to&nbsp;
blows, since Lucas disagrees with the way Jason&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:18.560
and the rest of the jocks are hunting Eddie&nbsp;
and the rest of the Hellfire Club in Vol. 1.

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:21.920
Although Lucas tries to expand&nbsp;
his social circle in Season 4,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:25.120
it's great to see him stay loyal&nbsp;
to his true friends. Hopefully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:28.640
Lucas beating Jason is the bully's&nbsp;
comeuppance for his arrogant behavior.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:32.080
It looks like the fight takes place&nbsp;
in the attic of the Creel house,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:37.120
an important place the gang has already visited&nbsp;
to look for clues about Victor Creel and Vecna.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:40.160
Clearly, this is going to be a&nbsp;
key location in the final battle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:44.480
because the trailer also shows Eleven screaming&nbsp;
in the Upside Down's version of the house.

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:50.400
Okay, it's time to talk about Nancy Wheeler and&nbsp;
Steve Harington. It's very clear in Vol. 1 that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:54.800
Nancy isn't sure whether she wants to continue&nbsp;
her relationship with Jonathan because of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:59.520
huge distance between them now that he's living&nbsp;
in California with Joyce, Will, and Eleven.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:05.040
But while she's mulling all this over, she starts&nbsp;
getting closer with Steve again... Interesting.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:08.960
The new trailer shows off a couple of moments&nbsp;
with Nancy and Steve making their way through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:13.760
the Upside Down, and it's clear they're trying to&nbsp;
keep each other safe. It's entirely possible that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:18.720
they'll get together in Vol. 2, and honestly we're&nbsp;
kind of rooting for it at this point — with one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:24.160
key reservation. Although they do make an adorable&nbsp;
couple, their love connection definitely spells&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:29.920
danger for the duo. "Stranger Things" never lets&nbsp;
us off with an uncomplicated happily ever after.

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:34.320
Robin delivers a particularly foreboding&nbsp;
line at the end of the trailer when she says&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:38.000
she has a terrible feeling that "it&nbsp;
might not work out for us this time."

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:41.200
Uh oh — surely that paints&nbsp;
a target on Steve's back?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:48.149
Thankfully there isn't long&nbsp;
to wait. "Stranger Things 4"&nbsp;&nbsp;Vol. 2 arrives on Netflix on July 1, 2022.

